WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.090 --> 00:00:02.910
A single hair, left behind.

2
00:00:02.960 --> 00:00:05.710
On it, a speck of DNA.

3
00:00:05.760 --> 00:00:07.660
Far too little to study.

4
00:00:07.710 --> 00:00:10.470
It needs to become billions of copies.

5
00:00:10.520 --> 00:00:14.340
Part of the answer comes from
a bacterium of hot springs.

6
00:00:14.390 --> 00:00:19.300
Its DNA polymerase is not
denatured at 95 degrees Celsius.

7
00:00:19.350 --> 00:00:22.970
So how can a speck of DNA
be copied into billions,

8
00:00:23.020 --> 00:00:25.150
and then sorted by size?

9
00:00:25.200 --> 00:00:28.890
In this mission, you'll build
PCR from its ingredients:

10
00:00:28.940 --> 00:00:34.820
template DNA, two primers, free
nucleotides and a heat-stable polymerase.

11
00:00:34.870 --> 00:00:38.440
Then you'll load DNA into
a gel, apply a voltage,

12
00:00:38.490 --> 00:00:40.790
and watch the fragments separate.

13
00:00:40.840 --> 00:00:45.840
Your mission: find out how a speck
of DNA becomes billions of copies,

14
00:00:45.890 --> 00:00:47.800
then gets sorted by size.
